Goal: add a --tsv flag to the CLI so tab-separated stdin is parsed with a tab separator, while behaviour without the flag stays exactly as it is now. Make one pull request.

Context (current repo state):
- bin/csv2json.js reads stdin with readFileSync(0, 'utf8'), calls parse(text) with no separator, writes JSON.stringify(result) plus '\n', and ignores process.argv.
- src/parse.js exports parse(text, sep = ','), which already splits each line on sep. Rows are split on /\r?\n/.
- test/csv.test.js uses node:test and has a 'cli' test that runs bin/csv2json.js through execFileSync with `input`.
- package.json has "test": "node --test".
- README.md shows only `node bin/csv2json.js < table.csv`.

Steps:
1. In bin/csv2json.js, check whether '--tsv' appears anywhere in process.argv.slice(2). If it does, call parse(text, '\t'); if not, call parse(text) exactly as today. Leave the output format alone (JSON.stringify with no indentation, then one '\n'). Don't change how unknown arguments are handled, and don't add --help, --sep or auto-detection.
2. Leave src/parse.js as it is unless you really need to change it. Fields are still split naively, with no quoting rules.
3. Add tests to test/csv.test.js (or a new test/*.test.js file) using node:test and execFileSync('node', ['bin/csv2json.js', '--tsv'], { input, encoding: 'utf8' }). Each test asserts exact output:
   - input 'a\tb\n1\t2\n' -> '[{"a":"1","b":"2"}]\n'
   - input 'name\tnote\nx\thello, world\n' -> '[{"name":"x","note":"hello, world"}]\n'
   - input 'a\tb\n1\t2\n3\t4\n' -> '[{"a":"1","b":"2"},{"a":"3","b":"4"}]\n'
   Also add a no-flag test: input 'a\tb\n1\t2\n' -> '[{"a\\tb":"1\\t2"}]\n' (the JSON text contains backslash-t escapes). Keep the existing CSV tests.
4. Update README.md: add a section that documents the --tsv flag, shows the example `node bin/csv2json.js --tsv < table.tsv`, and says the flag means the input is tab-separated (fields split on a tab). Keep the existing CSV example.
5. Check from the repo root before you open the PR:
   - printf 'a\tb\n1\t2\n' | node bin/csv2json.js --tsv; echo "exit=$?"  -> [{"a":"1","b":"2"}] then exit=0
   - printf 'name\tnote\nx\thello, world\n' | node bin/csv2json.js --tsv  -> [{"name":"x","note":"hello, world"}]
   - printf 'a\tb\n1\t2\n3\t4\n' | node bin/csv2json.js --tsv  -> [{"a":"1","b":"2"},{"a":"3","b":"4"}]
   - printf 'a,b\n1,2\n' | node bin/csv2json.js  -> [{"a":"1","b":"2"}]
   - printf 'a\tb\n1\t2\n' | node bin/csv2json.js  -> [{"a\tb":"1\t2"}]
   - npm test  -> exits 0
6. Commit and open one pull request that describes the change.